WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.760
Same procedure.

2
00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:01.450
Same patient.

3
00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:02.420
A different building.

4
00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:04.880
Office.

5
00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:05.850
Surgery center.

6
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:06.970
Hospital outpatient.

7
00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.050
One procedure.

8
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:09.890
One case.

9
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.160
Medicare's own published rates.

10
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.730
Office to hospital, plus one hundred sixty eight percent.

11
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.720
The building is the price.

12
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.000
Most health plans must file their contracted rates.

13
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.650
The files are public.

14
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.350
And huge.

15
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.260
Almost nobody on the buying side opens one.

16
00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:33.330
We read them.

17
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.890
That is the whole company.

18
00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:39.650
A sample too thin gets a refusal, not a number.

19
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.720
The first bad number you hand a chief financial officer is the last one they trust.

20
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.670
Brokers bring the page to the renewal table.

21
00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:52.650
General agencies hand it to every producer.

22
00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:57.360
Self-funded employers weigh one building against the next.

23
00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:00.160
Health plans see their filed rates beside the market.

24
00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:03.180
One flat fee.

25
00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:05.020
Never a share of anything.

26
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.130
Bring a procedure and a place.

27
00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:09.146
The door is open.
